        "text": "Good evening, and welcome to the weather report. Tomorrow will start cold and foggy in most parts of the country. In the north, temperatures will be around two degrees early in the morning, but by midday the fog will clear and we can expect sunshine. In the east, it will be cloudy all day, with light rain in the afternoon. On the south coast, the wind will be strong, especially near the sea, so ferries may be delayed. The west will be warm for the time of year, with temperatures up to fifteen degrees, but there will be heavy rain in the evening. Drivers should take care on the roads in the morning, because the fog can make it difficult to see. On Thursday, the weather will change. A cold front will arrive from the Atlantic, bringing snow to the mountains in the north. The snow will start in the afternoon, and by Friday morning there could be ten centimetres on high ground. The weekend looks drier and brighter, but it will stay cold. That's all for now. Goodnight."
